IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-3-versions-and-publication`

-- je21-tests-seat-3-versions-and-publication: tests for the exported questions about consolidated, revised and official versions, publication and privilege.
-- The expected values were written by hand from Articles 12 to 18 and 22 before the module was run.
-- The questions use the default reading of each fork, which je21-seat-defaults names; the other readings are tested in the rule modules' tests.

§ `Seat questions -- versions and publication -- tests`

§§ `Names for the changes and the texts`

`a change under Schedule 1(i)` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "words made gender neutral", `a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(i): to change words to make them gender neutral`
`a change under Article 14` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "a typographical error corrected", `a power in Article 14` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors`
`a change with no power named` MEANS `Change in a draft revision` OF "a change nobody has authority for", `no power is stated`
-- The five facts: its kind; Jersey legislation; carries the statement; website version; printed version.
`as-enacted text` MEANS `Facts about a text` OF `as-enacted legislation`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`consolidated text with the statement on the website` MEANS `Facts about a text` OF `consolidated legislation`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`consolidated text without the statement` MEANS `Facts about a text` OF `consolidated legislation`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`revised text printed with the statement` MEANS `Facts about a text` OF `revised legislation`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

§§ `Articles 12 and 13`

#ASSERT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is this text as-enacted legislation?` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this text consolidated legislation?` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this text consolidated legislation?` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is this text consolidated legislation?` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is commenced` (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is revised` (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `none of these has happened` (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE TRUE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` FALSE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 27)
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 28)
#ASSERT `Does Article 13(1) require a consolidated version of this legislation to be prepared?` TRUE FALSE `the legislation is amended` (YMD 2021 9 29)
#ASSERT `Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires?` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires?` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does this consolidated legislation carry the statement the Law requires?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 13(2) speaks of consolidated legislation, and the text is not consolidated legislation"

§§ `Article 14`

#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the removal of a provision relating to its commencement` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this editorial change?` `the correction of typographical and clerical errors` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 14(1) gives the power for consolidated legislation, and the Law does not say whether the Principal Legislative Drafter may make the change in any other text"
#ASSERT `Does this editorial change have effect in full?` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does this editorial change have effect in full?` TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 14(3) gives the power for formatting and presentational changes to consolidated legislation made so that it is consistent with current drafting practice, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may make the change otherwise"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter make this formatting or presentational change?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 14(3) gives the power for formatting and presentational changes to consolidated legislation made so that it is consistent with current drafting practice, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may make the change otherwise"
#ASSERT `Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must this change be set out in an endnote or other suitable place?` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` `a published version of as-enacted legislation, with an error that occurred after it was made`
#ASSERT `May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` `a published version of revised legislation, with an error that occurred after its revision`
#ASSERT REFUSED `May the Principal Legislative Drafter correct this error in a published version?` `any other published version or error` BECAUSE "Article 14(6) lets the Principal Legislative Drafter correct an error in a published version of as-enacted legislation that occurred after it was made, or of revised legislation that occurred after its revision, and the Law does not say whether the Drafter may correct any other"

§§ `Article 15 and Schedule 1`

#ASSERT `Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` (`a power in Schedule 1` `Schedule 1(c): to rearrange the provisions of legislation, or a list in a provision`)
#ASSERT `Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` (`a power in Article 14` `the correction of errors in grammar, spelling and punctuation`)
#ASSERT NOT `Is the power relied on for this change one the Law gives?` `no power is stated`
#ASSERT `Does the statement name a power for every change?` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change under Article 14`)
#ASSERT NOT `Does the statement name a power for every change?` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change with no power named`)
#ASSERT `Does the statement name a power for every change?` (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` (LIST `a change under Schedule 1(i)`, `a change under Article 14`)
#ASSERT NOT `Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` (LIST `a change with no power named`)
#ASSERT `Are all the changes in this draft revision within the powers of Article 14 or Schedule 1?` (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `May the Law Revision Board certify the draft revision as revised legislation?` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May the Law Revision Board certify the draft revision as revised legislation?` FALSE
#ASSERT `Do the changes made by a revision have effect as if made by an amendment in other legislation?` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Do the changes made by a revision have effect as if made by an amendment in other legislation?` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 15(8) speaks of the changes made by a revision, and the Law does not say what the changes in a draft that has not been certified do"
#ASSERT `Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` (YMD 2023 5 31) (YMD 2023 5 31)
#ASSERT `Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` (YMD 2023 5 30) (YMD 2023 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Did the Board lay its minutes before the States in time?` (YMD 2023 6 1) (YMD 2023 5 31)

§§ `Article 16`

#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2021 9 27)
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2021 9 28)
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2021 9 29)
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2019 1 1)
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2019 1 2)
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `revised legislation` (YMD 2018 12 31)
#ASSERT `Does Article 16(1) require this legislation to be published?` `revised legislation` (YMD 2020 6 1)
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `as-enacted legislation` (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 9 9) EQUALS YMD 2022 5 1
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2022 5 1) (YMD 2022 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2022 6 1
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `consolidated legislation` (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2022 6 1
#ASSERT `From what day must this legislation be published as soon as practicable?` `revised legislation` (YMD 2023 1 3) (YMD 2022 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2023 1 3

§§ `Articles 17 and 18`

#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` `as-enacted text`
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` `consolidated text with the statement on the website`
#ASSERT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` `revised text printed with the statement`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this text an official version of the legislation?` `consolidated text without the statement`
#ASSERT `Is the official version taken to set out the text of the as-enacted legislation correctly?` `as-enacted text`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is the official version taken to set out the text of the as-enacted legislation correctly?` `consolidated text with the statement on the website` BECAUSE "Article 17(3) speaks of an official version of as-enacted legislation, and this text is not as-enacted legislation"
#ASSERT `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` `consolidated text with the statement on the website` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` `revised text printed with the statement` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` `consolidated text with the statement on the website` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` `consolidated text without the statement` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 17(4) speaks of an official version of consolidated legislation, and Article 17(2) does not make this text one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is the official version taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly?` `consolidated text with the statement on the website` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 17(4) speaks only of the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated, and the Law does not say what the text is taken to set out for any other date"
#ASSERT `Is this text admissible in evidence?` `as-enacted text`
#ASSERT `Is this text admissible in evidence?` `consolidated text with the statement on the website`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is this text admissible in evidence?` `consolidated text without the statement` BECAUSE "Article 17(5) speaks of an official version of legislation, and Article 17(1) and (2) do not make this text one; the Law does not say whether any other text is admissible"
#ASSERT `Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` `as-enacted text`
#ASSERT `Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` `revised text printed with the statement`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Must a court take judicial notice of this text?` `consolidated text without the statement` BECAUSE "Article 17(5) speaks of an official version of legislation, and Article 17(1) and (2) do not make this text one; the Law does not say whether a court must take notice of any other text"
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation`
#ASSERT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment uses a power set out in Schedule 1`
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these`
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 18 give Statute Law Revision Regulations the power to make this amendment?` FALSE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation`
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these`
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation`
-- A proposition that is not for Regulations under Article 18 is outside the bar; see the rule module's tests (NOTES.md section 10.3).
#ASSERT `Is this amendment to the proposition not barred from being lodged by Article 18(3)?` FALSE TRUE TRUE `the amendment rests on none of these`
#ASSERT `May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` TRUE FALSE
-- A provision a Law could not make: the paragraph gives no power and the Law says nothing else; see the rule module's tests (NOTES.md section 10.3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `May Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 18(4) lets Statute Law Revision Regulations make any provision that could be made by a Law, and the Law does not say whether they may make a provision that a Law could not"

§§ `Article 22`

#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`Facts about a provider of instructions` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `the Principal Legislative Drafter` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` FALSE
#ASSERT `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`Facts about a provider of instructions` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `a trainee Legislative Drafter` `any other communication` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`Facts about a provider of instructions` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `a trainee Legislative Drafter` `any other communication` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`Facts about a provider of instructions` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `the Principal Legislative Drafter` `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Are my communications with the Legislative Drafting Office privileged?` (`Facts about a provider of instructions` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `none of these` `an unpublished draft of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the Legislative Drafting Office` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 22 gives legal professional privilege to confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter, and the Law says nothing of other communications"
